**Purpose:** Provide continuity context for new AI assistant sessions. This rule is loaded automatically (alwaysApply) so the agent has project and recent-work context without reading a separate file.

## Project Overview

This repo is an **agentic workflow template**: Beads for issue/memory, Agent Mail MCP for coordination, Cursor rules for conventions. It can be copied as the basis for another project (e.g. Django blog). Work is tracked in Beads; agents run `bd ready`, claim tasks, and close beads. Key docs and scripts live under `docs/`, `scripts/`, and `bin/`.

## Key Locations

| Location | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `AGENTS.md` | Top-level agent instructions (Beads loop, project goal) |
| `TODO.md` | Follow-up tasks and evaluations (bjn analysis, skills.sh, etc.) |
| `docs/` | Project docs (BJN-CURSOR-ANALYSIS.md, MULTI-AGENT-READINESS.md, etc.); conventions and workflow are in .cursor/rules/ |
| `.cursor/rules/` | Cursor rules (agentic-workflow, project-context, django-blog, Agent Mail, handover-context, handover-management) |
| `.cursor/mcp.json` | MCP config (project-local only; Agent Mail server) |
| `.beads/` | Beads DB and config; run `./bin/bd` from repo root |
| `scripts/` | `ensure_agent_mail.sh`, `test_agent_mail.sh` (run from repo root) |
| `bin/` | `bd` binary (Beads CLI) |
| `mcp_agent_mail/` | Agent Mail MCP server (submodule); venv, .env |

